Every hit uses the same slot lookup result that would be
obtained for this exact receiver class at the current epoch.
Eviction cannot change behavior because a miss recomputes that
lookup. Two entries can be probed in constant time, but
cycling through three classes can cause eviction on every
call. A concurrent version needs a publication and lifetime
protocol so a method cannot be replaced between a version
check and invocation in a way the dispatch semantics forbid.
